Reconnect pods only for demand or active agents

Connecting to a host or entering a pod must not wake every idle sibling.
Resume a pod only for an explicit connection request, a live frontend or
reconnect subscriber, or an agent last observed processing. Keep healthy
idle transports open, but leave idle and unknown pods dormant after
loss. Remove Kubernetes sibling recovery and persist observed processing
activity so daemon startup restores only those pods, on any backend.

Expire one-shot connection requests after both event and git transports
are ready. Release subscriber demand when its response closes, and keep
Codex frontend demand scoped to its process. Protect persisted activity
and restored resources against late results from stop or recreation.

Share two transport setup slots per host as a secondary burst limit.
Successful handshakes release capacity immediately; failed or cancelled
attempts retain slots for a 500 ms cooldown. Release event admission at
HTTP headers, before readiness that may depend on git repair. Skip busy
foreground git setup and back off streams that close after a greeting.

Cover selective SSH recovery, dormant frontend subscriptions, persisted
processing activity, stale observations, fast success, failure cooldown,
and readiness that depends on queued git repair.
